  "query_preview": "..\nKey Message 1...Valley fog is possible tonight. \n\nSurface high pressure centered over the central Great \nLakes will support rather dry condition to persist across WNY \nthrough Saturday. Additionally, ample radiational cooling from clear \nskies under the high tonight will support valley fog across the \nSouthern Tier, the Finger Lakes, the Black River and across areas \nsoutheast of Lake Ontario.\n\nKey Message 2...The potential for scattered showers and \nthunderstorms increases Saturday night into Sunday. Shower chances \nthen linger through Monday.\n\nUpper level ridging currently across the Upper Great Lakes will work \nits way east this weekend, allowing for zonal flow and embedded \nshortwave troughs to pass across the eastern Great Lakes by late \nSaturday. Meanwhile at the surface, a warm front will work its way \neastward across the Great Lakes reaching WNY Saturday night. Warm \nmoist isentropic lift will support scattered showers to pass \neastward across the area Saturday night into Sunday. In addition to \nthe showers, some rumbles of thunder can't be ruled out as there \nwill be enough elevated instability.\n\nAdditional shortwave troughs will pass overhead Sunday and Sunday \nnight, supporting the cold front associated with the low supporting \nthe aforementioned warm front to pass across the region. Along and \nahead of the cold frontal passage, expect additional showers and \nthunderstorms. While conditions will be favorable for a few storms \nto become severe given moderate instability and moderate to strong \ndeep-layer bulk shear, severe storm development will be contingent \non a few factors, the biggest one being the degree of diurnal \ndestabilization of the warm sector.\n\nWhile a ridge will build back into the area Monday, temperatures \naloft will cool to around 10C. This combined with the 24C lake \nwaters along with lingering synoptic moisture may support a few lake \neffect rain showers to develop southeast of Lakes Erie and Ontario.",
